<Base title="Free home planning tools" description="Try free patio planning tools: arrange furniture and privacy screens in 3D, or visualize tile cuts and estimate pieces and boxes."><header class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A little help with the planning</p><h1>Useful tools.<br/><em>Thoughtful starting points.</em></h1><p class="lead">Simple ways to make a decision before buying. No account required.</p></header><section class="container section tool-feature"><div><h2>Patio &amp; Balcony Layout Planner</h2><p>See how your balcony or patio could come together. Add walls, doors, windows, seating, storage, and plants. Drag pieces into place and compare privacy screens with regular or uneven gaps. Save or print your layout.</p><a class="button" href="/tools/patio-privacy-planner/">Open the planner ↗</a></div><img src="/assets/planner-layout-example.webp" alt="Example from our 3D planner: a patio with two chairs, a table, storage benches, potted plants, walls, doors, windows, and privacy screens." width="898" height="725" loading="lazy"/></section><section class="container section tool-feature tile-tool-feature"><div><p class="eyebrow">New · Plan the floor</p><h2>Patio Tile Layout Planner</h2><p>See full tiles and edge cuts. Compare corner and centered grids, rotate rectangular tiles, and estimate pieces and boxes from your own measurements. Each cut position gets its own source tile; no hidden offcut reuse.</p><a class="button" href="/tools/patio-tile-planner/">Plan a tile layout →</a></div><img src="/assets/tile-planner-example.svg" alt="Measured tile layout with green full tiles and hatched cut pieces around the edges." width="764" height="622" loading="lazy"/></section></Base>
